## C6 — Magnitude: the 1D correction is **+207.0 nats per unit h**, 94.7% of events positive, and it opposes the 1D rail almost exactly. [LOCAL — measured this session]

Probe: `.planning/derivation-gfrac-20260805/n2_sphi_tilt.py` →
`n2_sphi_tilt_results.json`. Built the production `S̄_φ(z;h)` table
(`precompute_phi_marginal_survival`, mix200k pool, 41-h grid) and evaluated
`ln S̄_φ` at the GW-peak redshift `z*(d_L,det;h)` for all 1590 CRB events
(point-GW approximation; completion-leg-dominated events).

| quantity | value |
|---|---|
| `S̄_φ` at the GW peak, h=0.73 | median **0.266**, 5–95% [0.031, 0.899], min 1.9e-4 |
| per-event `dln S̄_φ/dh` @0.73 | median **+0.1398**, 5–95% [−0.0008, +0.2105], **94.7% positive** |
| **Σ over 1590 events** | **+207.0 nats/h** (chord over the full grid +207.8 ⇒ essentially linear) |
| effective exponent `dln S̄_φ/dln(1+z*)` | **+0.375** (cf. `g`'s `−s_dex = +0.43`) |
| median `z*` @0.73 | 0.490 |

Comparison objects, from the same run of record
(`results/run_20260804_postfix/{iiib,joint_r1}/combined_{1d,2d}.json`, read this
session):

| venue · channel | MAP | ln-posterior chord slope 0.60→0.73 |
|---|---|---|
| iiib 1D | 0.600 (rail) | **−247.4 nats/h** |
| joint_r1 1D | 0.600 (rail) | **−184.0 nats/h** |
| iiib 2D | 0.780 | +267.9 |
| joint_r1 2D | 0.800 | +251.9 |

⇒ adding +207 nats/h to the 1D channel removes **84%** of the iiib 1D down-tilt
and **over-corrects** joint_r1's (−184 → +24, sign flip off the rail). The 2D
channel is predicted to move by ≈0.

**This is a log-slope comparison, not a MAP decomposition.** The standing
never-add-MAP-displacements rule (`GATE_PACKAGE_FINAL.md:609`;
`DERIVATION_C7_HOSTZ_KERNEL.md:545-547`; enforced when it refuted
`GFRAC_DERIVATION_PACKAGE.md` §7 at
[`GATEB_REFUTATION_REPORT.md`](../../../.planning/derivation-gfrac-20260805/GATEB_REFUTATION_REPORT.md)
row 4) applies: tilts add in ln-space, MAPs do not.

**Carried holes (do not over-quote C6):**
(i) the point-GW approximation ignores the quadrature's z-width — it is a
first-order read, not a delivered posterior;
(ii) it applies the completion-leg correction to *all* 1590 events, i.e. it
assumes completion dominance (measured only for the 2D channel: 95%,
`GFRAC_DERIVATION_PACKAGE.md` §6.6 — **the 1D mixture share was not measured**);
(iii) the catalogue leg's own correction (C8) is omitted entirely.

**Refute by:** the counterfactual toggle (derivation draft §6) — a default-off
`--selection_in_completion_numerator` instrumentation run at both venues on the
41-h grid. `Σ Δln(1D)` must reproduce +207 ± tail correction, and the 2D channel
must be bit-identical up to the `σ_cond` residual. Both are pre-registered there.

